    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d261">

                <pb facs="1310" n="1152" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1152"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Jackson</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May 3,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11, Montenegrin series.</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 30, Montenegrin series, of the 4th ultimo, informing the department that the
                    Montenegrin minister of foreign affairs has asked you to inform him “if the
                    Government of the United States is disposed to prohibit, on request from the
                    Montenegrin Government, the admission into the United States of any Montenegrins
                    presenting themselves without passports regularly viséed for the purpose of
                    emigration to America.”</p>
                <p>Your reply to the effect that this Government would not be willing to comply with
                    such a request is approved. The administrative officers of the United States may
                    exclude only the classes of persons whose entry is prohibited by law.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
